.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- create or update the notification system's Python virtual environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run from any directory; the script changes to the repository root first.
It creates
.I venv/
with
.B $PYTHON
when absent, upgrades
.BR pip ,
installs
.I requirements.txt
(runtime dependencies plus Authlib, pyzmq and pytest), installs this package
in editable mode, and, when a sibling checkout
.I ../mu2edaq-discovery
exists, installs that in editable mode too so the server can announce itself.
It finally creates
.I data/
and
.IR core/ .
Safe to re\-run. A re\-run installs anything missing but does not upgrade a
package that already satisfies its specifier: only
.B pip
itself is installed with
.BR \-\-upgrade .
.PP
Linux and macOS only. On Windows 11 create the environment by hand with
.B py \-m venv venv
and
.BR "venv\eScripts\epip install \-r requirements.txt \-e ." .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I requirements.txt
Dependencies installed into the environment.
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment (gitignored).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Interpreter used to create
.I venv/
(default
.BR python3 ;
3.9 or newer).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; non\-zero, from the failing command, when venv creation or any
.B pip
step fails
.RB ( "set \-euo pipefail" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
PYTHON=python3.9 ./bootstrap.sh
venv/bin/pytest \-q
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
.BR mu2edaq-phone-notification-system .
